Usage: cut OPTION... [FILE]...

Print selected parts of lines from each FILE to standard output.

OPTIONS:
  -b, --bytes ARG                   select only these bytes
  -c, --characters ARG              select only these characters
  -d, --delimiter ARG               use DELIM instead of TAB for field delimiter
  -w, --whitespace-delimited[=ARG]  use runs of spaces/tabs as field delimiters
                                    [=trimmed]
  -f, --fields ARG                  select only these fields
  -F ARG                            like -f, but also implies -w and -O ' '
      --complement                  complement the set of selected bytes,
                                    characters or fields
  -n, --no-partial                  do not split multibyte characters in byte
                                    mode [DIFFERS: GNU ignores -n]
  -s, --only-delimited              do not print lines not containing delimiter
  -O, --output-delimiter ARG        use STRING as the output delimiter
  -z, --zero-terminated             line delimiter is NUL, not newline
  -M                                compatibility option; not supported on
                                    Windows
      --help                        display this help and exit
  -V, --version                     output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
